    "summary": "Artefact comprising two teeth-shaped pieces of ivory attached by length of &#039;Z&#039; twist sinew to a seal figure carved in two parts (each perforated with two holes through which the sinew string passes). The two halves of the seal, a toggle, are engraved with eyes and physical features, circles, and each section is pierced with two holes for attachment, originally perhaps to seal-skin line. The two teeth shaped ornaments are similarly engraved with concentric lines.",
